From a38c916385a1f1b876a8a98bd3b87b9fe5981774 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thatjuan <juan@cxdmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 19:29:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] licenses: record the Go modules pkg.go.dev rate-limits

A stamped build fails when a dependency has no licence. Pixie's fetcher reads
Go licences that GitHub cannot classify from pkg.go.dev, 12 at a time, and
pkg.go.dev refuses enough of them that 28 to 35 came back empty on every
build, a different set each time (oramasearch/orama-operator#455).

These are the 143 modules the fetcher can only get from pkg.go.dev, read from
it one at a time; the check itself is unchanged.
---
 tools/licenses/manual_licenses.json | 1049 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 1025 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/licenses/manual_licenses.json b/tools/licenses/manual_licenses.json
index 0ac46e247..568fb1d72 100644
--- a/tools/licenses/manual_licenses.json
+++ b/tools/licenses/manual_licenses.json
